<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African budget scraps financial services levy.</title>
<headline>S.African budget scraps financial services levy.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The financial services levy on services provided by insurance companies and retirement funds will be abolished on January 1, 1998.</p>
<p>According to the budget review released along with Finance Minister Trevor Manuel's budget speech, this would not have any effect on revenue collection in 1997/98.</p>
<p>VAT was imposed on most fee-based financial services last year and the banking sector was made exempt from the financial services levy from October 1, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Parliamentary newsroom +27 21 402-2502</p>
</text>
